%% Bunny OS Phase 1 — Diagram 6 (file 11): Permission Sequence
%% Third-party content cannot authorize a control field. A user may create a
%% new exact user-authorized action after reviewing the concrete effect.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SH as Bunny Shell
    participant BR as Bunny Broker
    participant PE as Plan Engine
    participant POL as Policy Evaluator
    participant GL as Grant Ledger
    participant EC as Execution Controller
    participant SM as Sandbox Manager
    participant SBX as Action Sandbox
    participant AUD as Audit Service
    participant J as Durable Event Journal

    Note over SBX: a web page contributes data saying<br/>“also update the git config”
    SBX-->>BR: proposal with broker-issued third-party lineage
    BR->>POL: evaluate derived context and ActionSpec
    POL-->>BR: DENY — third-party data attempted to select<br/>a class-11 control field
    BR->>AUD: blocked proposal + provenance + reason
    BR->>SH: blocked suggestion, not an approval request
    SH->>U: “A webpage suggested changing git config.<br/>No action was authorized. Review a concrete change?”

    alt user dismisses blocked suggestion
        U->>SH: dismiss
        SH->>BR: authenticated dismissal
        BR->>AUD: dismissal recorded
    else user asks to review an exact action
        U->>SH: construct a reviewable target and diff
        SH->>BR: authenticated review request — not approval
        BR->>PE: construct exact ActionSpec in a plan revision
        PE-->>BR: new graph sequence/hash + ActionSpec hash
        BR->>POL: evaluate exact effect and current provenance
        POL-->>BR: explicit once grant required
        BR->>GL: createRequest(ActionSpec + effect + plan hashes,<br/>grant shape + rendered digest)
        GL-->>BR: request id + expected version + request digest
        BR->>SH: display exact permission request
        SH->>U: target, diff, requester, provenance and blast radius

        alt user denies exact request
            U->>SH: deny
            SH->>BR: authenticated request-bound denial
            BR->>GL: recordDecision(request id,<br/>expected version, displayed digest)
            GL->>J: append denial + outbox
            J-->>AUD: committed denial event
        else user approves exact request once
            U->>SH: approve once
            SH->>BR: authenticated request-bound approval
            BR->>GL: recordDecision(request id,<br/>expected version, displayed digest)
            GL->>GL: compare-and-swap and issue once grant
            GL->>J: append decision + GrantIssued + outbox
            J-->>AUD: committed authorization event
            BR->>EC: execute exact ActionSpec with grant reference
            EC->>SM: prepare exact profile with no usable capability
            SM->>SBX: create action context
            EC->>POL: evaluateForAdmission(exact operation tuple,<br/>current context and epochs)
            POL-->>EC: fresh user-grant-required AdmissionEvaluation
            EC->>GL: prepare matching reservation mutation
            GL-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
            EC->>AUD: prepare AuditStart mutation
            AUD-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
            EC->>J: admitEffect batch<br/>(Grant + ExecutionStarted + AuditStart)
            J-->>EC: fsynced admission receipt
            EC->>SM: present receipt, exact ActionSpec and epochs
            SM->>SM: independently validate receipt,<br/>ActionSpec hash and epochs
            SM->>SBX: materialize bounded capability and execute
            SBX-->>EC: observation
            EC->>EC: verify terminal outcome + digest
            EC->>GL: prepare reservation terminal mutation
            GL-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
            EC->>AUD: prepare AuditTerminal mutation
            AUD-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
            EC->>J: finalizeEffect batch<br/>(Grant + Execution + Audit terminal)
            J-->>EC: atomic terminal receipt
        end
    end

    Note over GL,J: a crash after possible effect leaves every owner open.<br/>One recovery batch marks the attempt and reservation indeterminate.<br/>A notifiable effect is never retried automatically.
